hould be displayed.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Value-swift.struct\/init(value:symbol:text:position:font:color:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/value-swift.struct\/init(value:symbol:text:position:font:color:)"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/SymbolValue":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/symbolvalue","role":"symbol","title":"MXLDegree.SymbolValue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/SymbolValue","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SymbolValue","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The degree-symbol-value type indicates which symbol should be used in specifying a degree.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SymbolValue","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"title":"MXLFont","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont